u rho(y): (-p, -p, -p*(A + p))
Int(g) rho u(y): (-p, -p, -p*(-2*B + p + 1)/2)
Twice central difference: -p*(2*A + 2*B + p - 1)
For p a profinite unit: A+B=(1-p)/2; beta=(p-1)/2.
The commutator-normalized f=y^B g^-1 x^A is gauge-invariant.
Complex conjugation p=-1,g=y: f=1,beta=-1.
No pentagon follows from this normalization alone.
